          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-20869 tests: always run sanity 123a loop exit checks",
        "message": "LU-20869 tests: always run sanity 123a loop exit checks\n\ntest_123a_base grows the file count by 10x per round and\nis meant to stop once a round takes more than a few\nseconds. The checks that stop it were placed after a\n\"continue\" taken whenever the statahead run measured 0\nseconds, so the loop skipped them and went on to 10000\nfiles whenever statahead finished in under a second. That\nround costs about two minutes for ls -l without statahead\nplus a long unlink, so 123aa/ab/ac/ad ran either ~35s or\n~300s per call depending on timer rounding.\n\nOnly skip the \"slower with statahead\" comparison when a\ntiming is zero, and always run the loop termination\nchecks. Statahead is still exercised at each size, and\n123ad separately checks 10000 files with statahead.\n\n123aa on a local VM cluster: before 35s and 300s, after\n60s and 85s (both stop at 1000 files; the 1000 file\nno-statahead pass itself varied 11s to 24s).\n123aa/ab/ac/ad run the loop 1, 1, 2 and 2 times.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity env=ONLY=\"123aa 123ab 123ac 123ad\"\nFixes: f46cee3d0b75 (\"Branch HEAD b=15691 i=eric.mei i=peng.ye\")\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Id2131fcba3e605c28e1c4ecabe46e71f2c445d7b\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
